text:
{
  "opening": "This release introduces several new recipes and functions to extend the capabilities of more-itertools, including polynomial evaluation, combination indexing, and relative seeking. It also corrects behaviors in existing functions like `unique_in_window` and `partial_product` to align with their documented specifications. Please ensure all public APIs are exposed as specified and behave according to the observable requirements below.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m04",
      "text": "The `relative_seek` function must be available and allow seeking within a seekable stream relative to the current position. The `seekable` class must support this relative seeking capability."
    },
    {
      "id": "m06",
      "text": "The `combination_index`, `combination_with_replacement_index`, `permutation_index`, and `product_index` functions must return the zero-based index of a given combination or permutation within its lexicographically sorted sequence. These functions should accept iterables representing the elements and return an integer index."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09",
      "text": "The `polynomial_eval` function must evaluate a polynomial at a given value, where the polynomial is represented by a list of coefficients. The `factor` and `sieve` functions must remain available for number theory operations."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10",
      "text": "The `nth_combination_with_replacement` function must return the nth combination with replacement from the input iterable, using lexicographic ordering. The `all_unique`, `nth_permutation`, and `value_chain` functions must continue to operate as previously defined."
    },
    {
      "id": "m11",
      "text": "The `sum_of_squares` function must return the sum of the squares of the items in the input iterable. The `convolve`, `matmul`, `polynomial_eval`, `polynomial_from_roots`, `sieve`, `take`, and `transpose` functions must maintain their existing behaviors and signatures."
    },
    {
      "id": "m12",
      "text": "The `iterate` function must yield results of repeatedly applying a function to the previous result, starting from an initial value. It should produce an infinite iterator unless a stop condition is provided."
    },
    {
      "id": "m15",
      "text": "The `partial_product` function must correctly generate partial products of the input iterables, fixing previous incorrect behavior. The `gray_product` function must remain available and functional."
    },
    {
      "id": "m19",
      "text": "The `unique_in_window` function must yield unique items from the input iterable, ensuring that each item is only yielded if it has not appeared in the most recent window of size n. The `duplicates_everseen` function must continue to track duplicates across the entire iteration."
    },
    {
      "id": "m20",
      "text": "The `polynomial_derivative` function must compute the derivative of a polynomial represented by a list of coefficients. The `matmul`, `polynomial_from_roots`, `sliding_window`, and `sum_of_squares` functions must retain their existing functionality."
    },
    {
      "id": "m22",
      "text": "The library must expose version 10.0.0 compatible interfaces for `batched`, `convolve`, `factor`, `matmul`, `numeric_range`, `sieve`, and `transpose`. These functions must adhere to the updated signatures and behaviors required for this major version release."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please verify that all listed public names are accessible from the top-level module and that their behaviors match the descriptions above. Ensure no regressions occur in existing functions during these updates."
}
